10650 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Concurrency control -> It is a process of mananging multiple users access and modification in data simultaneously in shared or multi-user database systems.)
/Pg 475 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
10651 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (How it helps?)
/Pg 475 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
10652 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 17199 0 R
/ActualText (Data Consistency: Ensures that data remains accurate and reliable despite concurrent access.)
/Pg 475 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
10653 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 17200 0 R
/ActualText (Isolation: Maintains the isolation property of transactions, so the outcome of a transaction is not affected by other concurrently executing transactions.)
/Pg 475 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
10654 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 17201 0 R
/ActualText (Serializability: Ensures that the result of concurrent transactions is the same as if the transactions had been executed serially)
/Pg 475 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
